<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bandar-e Anzali</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anzali, Enzeli, Bandar-e Pahlavi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bandar-e Anzali is a port city on the southern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Long Iran's main Caspian port for trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, it was called Bandar-e <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavi</a> between 1935 and 1979. In May 1920 a Bolshevik naval force landed there in pursuit of White Russian ships, an event that led to the proclamation of the Persian Socialist Soviet Republic in Gilan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bandar-e-anzali.jpg" alt="Bandar-e Anzali" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahad Tarassoudy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1%D9%87_%DA%AF%D9%85%D8%B1%DA%A9_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
